{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00649",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.2,
      "end_seconds": 10.71,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "G'day, doctor. I'll be honest, I'm a bit freaked out. My wife filmed me sleeping and I stop breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.3,
      "end_seconds": 19.9,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "That would worry anyone. Tell me what the video showed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.86,
      "end_seconds": 35.96,
      "duration_seconds": 15.1,
      "text": "I snore like a chainsaw, and then it goes quiet for, I don't know, ten seconds, then I make this awful snorting gasp. Over and over."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.8,
      "end_seconds": 41.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "How long has the snoring been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.99,
      "end_seconds": 50.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "Years, but the pauses are new, she only noticed this month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.28,
      "end_seconds": 56.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Do you wake up tired?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.09,
      "end_seconds": 63.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Wrecked. I'm dozing at traffic lights. That's what really scares me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.87,
      "end_seconds": 70.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Any morning headaches, or a dry mouth when you wake?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.64,
      "end_seconds": 80.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.67,
      "text": "No headaches, no. Dry mouth, yeah, a bit, but no headaches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.51,
      "end_seconds": 88.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Do you ever wake up choking or gasping?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.37,
      "end_seconds": 99.27,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "No, I don't think I wake up. She says I just gasp and carry on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.3,
      "end_seconds": 104.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Is your nose blocked at night?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.11,
      "end_seconds": 111.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Always. Both sides. I breathe through my mouth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.87,
      "end_seconds": 117.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Any allergies, to medicines especially?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.32,
      "end_seconds": 130.85,
      "duration_seconds": 12.53,
      "text": "Oh, something gave me a swollen lip once, years ago, but I don't know what it was. A tablet, I think. Or maybe food."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.36,
      "end_seconds": 145.01,
      "duration_seconds": 12.65,
      "text": "So possibly an allergic reaction, but you can't say what to. I'll note it as uncertain. Do you drink in the evenings?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.25,
      "end_seconds": 151.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "A couple of beers, most nights. I know, I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.42,
      "end_seconds": 164.97,
      "duration_seconds": 10.55,
      "text": "That relaxes the throat muscles and makes snoring worse. Let me look at your nose and throat. Say ahh. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.69,
      "end_seconds": 183.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "Ahhh."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.39,
      "end_seconds": 193.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.06,
      "text": "Your nostrils are swollen inside, and the throat's crowded at the back. That's why you're snoring. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.63,
      "end_seconds": 198.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Is it sleep apnoea, then? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.07,
      "end_seconds": 209.85,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "What you describe, loud snoring, pauses in breathing, and daytime sleepiness, looks most like obstructive sleep apnoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.98,
      "end_seconds": 214.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Right. Is that serious? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.05,
      "end_seconds": 228.73,
      "duration_seconds": 12.68,
      "text": "It can be, over time, and it's a real safety risk if you're drowsy driving. So I want to be definite about the next steps. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.04,
      "end_seconds": 233.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "What do I do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.77,
      "end_seconds": 242.09,
      "duration_seconds": 7.32,
      "text": "I'll refer you to the sleep clinic for a proper sleep study."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.64,
      "end_seconds": 248.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "How long will that take? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.43,
      "end_seconds": 264.82,
      "duration_seconds": 14.39,
      "text": "A few weeks, I'm afraid. Meanwhile, I'd like to start you on a nasal spray, fluticasone, two sprays in each nostril once a day, to open your nose up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.3,
      "end_seconds": 270.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Okay. Will that fix it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.44,
      "end_seconds": 283.68,
      "duration_seconds": 11.24,
      "text": "It won't cure sleep apnoea, but it can help the snoring, and make any treatment easier. Give it a fortnight. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.76,
      "end_seconds": 289.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "What about the driving? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.52,
      "end_seconds": 301.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.76,
      "text": "Please don't drive when you feel drowsy, pull over and take a break. And cut the beer in the evenings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.13,
      "end_seconds": 305.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Fair. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.19,
      "end_seconds": 320.99,
      "duration_seconds": 13.8,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in three weeks, to see how the nose is and where the sleep clinic has got to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.54,
      "end_seconds": 326.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Three weeks. Brilliant, thanks, doc. ~"
    }
  ]
}
